Well, let me tell you how to play flame mages and ice mages,
respectively, in SLASH'EM.

First, use your pet(s).  Train them until they are strong enough to
kill the watchmen and even the watchmen captains in the mall or in the
town in the gnomish mines.  That is, in the very first phase of your
game, play like a pacifist and only use your quarterstaff or magic in
emergencies.

Second, the watchmen captains will either drop long swords or silver
sabers.  Use those weapons, as you can train long sword up to "skilled"
and flame mages can even use silver sabers up to "skilled".  You can
even two-weapon with flame/ice mages up to "skilled", so play them like
typical fighter mages.  You will then even have some decent armour from
the watchmen (captains).  But still, always have your now strong pet
near, since flame/ice mages typically don't have good strength,
dexterity, and constitution values in the beginning.

Third, at some experience level you can polymorph into a red/white
dragon, so you can wander around in dragon form (but I don't use that).

That way I played a very powerful lawful flame mage, who was
two-weaponing the Sword of Justice and Excalibur, killed most monsters
in just one turn, and in addition had very powerful fire magic.

